+# B20-R-SERVICE-EVIDENCE — dated synthetic service history
+
+Only S05/S06 fresh controller releases are extended. Existing `runtime-v1.json`, imported candidate schedules/owners/routes and retained graphs are unchanged. The controller-only `data/scenarios/service-evidence-v1.json` explicitly authors one-occurrence service-log observations; it is not runtime tool input or real municipal history. Agent/MCP file isolation blocks this file and all unreleased scenario data.
+
+Canonical `PickupExecution` and `PICKUP_FOR` are reused. There was no existing runtime execution writer; a narrow controller call now compiles these records with a typed `SERVICE_EXECUTION_SOURCE`, hashed provenance/receipt companion and durable `GRAPH_EVIDENCE_CHANGED` native event through existing migration0005 Storage/fencing. No generic writer, ledger, endpoint, migration, role, operational intervention or package is added.
+
+Each source binds the actual collection point, route, investigation/incident, specific scheduled occurrence, checked/actual occurrence time, recording/review time, authenticated DEPT-SAN operator and distinct authenticated ANALYST reviewer. It validates against the actual B09 reviewed inspection report/journal, original request scope and canonical native/relationship hashes. Caller-supplied verified/reviewer/status fields are not accepted by B19 controls. Same-source identity cannot create a second execution. Routes are checked against actual inventory context, without promoting imported candidate recurring route/schedule assignments.
+
+For these explicitly synthetic fixtures the service due is120seconds before release, the separate service log is checked60seconds before release, and the later waste/deposit inspection observations occur at release. These offsets are authored fixture facts, not inferred travel times or a real lateness standard. The service log is not represented as an inspection performed before its lifecycle started: the inspection's own observations stay at/after its actual start. `scheduled_at` is a specifically attributed service-log due occurrence; candidate `HAS_SCHEDULE` remains CANDIDATE. No actual quantities are supplied or invented.
+
+S05 PRIMARY has an explicit reviewed MISSED log result (no actual_at); field evidence of persisted waste is separate from the unchanged qualitative capacity observation. S05 NEGATIVE has UNKNOWN service, no PickupExecution, and no invented missed event. S06 has separately sourced COMPLETED pickup/actual_at before the later field report; PRIMARY includes reviewed discriminating deposit/dumping observations, NEGATIVE includes completion only and supplies no dumping support. Equal/reversed/unknown timing, absent execution, wrong target/source/route or source mutation cannot qualify the chronology. Absence remains an evidence gap.
+
+New MISSED_PICKUP/ILLEGAL_DUMPING assessments in controller-bound S05/S06 investigations use rule3 (the compatible format2 classification envelope). This selection comes from the hashed demo/current investigation binding, not caller labels. It requires typed current service provenance before assigning causal service/sequence support or contradiction. Other investigations retain accepted rule2 qualitative-field semantics; rule2 is not proof of pickup-before-later-deposit history. Old rule1/2 assessments remain parseable/immutable. Source records remain context references, not causal support merely because they exist. The actual approved discriminating observations, occurrence scope and existing independence criteria still apply; one log/report does not establish independently VERIFIED cause or resolution.
+
+Existing `get_pickup_execution_history` MCP returns canonical executions and the source evidence, with normal cutoff/window/lookahead/RO protections and current service provenance validation. `PARTIAL` plus gaps when no history is available remains truthful. GET `/api/v1/evidence/{id}` and `evidence get --id` expose a closed optional `service_record` on validated service sources; raw private journals are withheld. Matching department readers remain scoped through the original inspected report. Other evidence DTOs keep the optional field empty. API consumers may regenerate types for this compatible optional field; no frontend work was performed.
+
+Collection complete does not imply waste resolved or illegal dumping. Existing B14-2 monitoring and independent post-service opportunity requirements are unchanged. No plan, approval, work order or outcome is fabricated by release. Capacity/route/dumping intervention gaps remain open.
+
+A report commit precedes the narrow service batch; the service source/execution/companion/event are atomic under the existing fence. A later readback or stage/transport failure can leave real committed evidence while the overall release is uncertain. Existing HTTP intent and demo reservation remain recovery-required; exact original-key replay blocks redispatch. Inspect the original request, report/B09 COMMITTED journal, typed service source/companion and native event. Successful reads do not clear the intent. Do not retry, replace keys, delete records, roll back or clear quarantine automatically. This change does not introduce a recovery subsystem.
+
+Focused reproduction, actual IDs/timestamps/provenance, zero-provider reports and known limitations are recorded under `docs/evidence/B20R-SERVICE-EVIDENCE-*`. Explicit synthetic operator commands and real DB/SDK/MCP/API/CLI are distinguished from genuine AI; no model solver or live provider was used. STOP for review; full B20 and B10 genuine acceptance remain open.
